<!--
  GlpSplitProtocol — the tiny shared client↔engine wire-protocol library for the
  061 REPL/engine split (feature 061, T001). Payload kind bytes + request/response
  codec over the shipped FrameCodec (contracts/wire-protocol.md).

  CLOBBER-SAFE (same rule as GlpLink/GlpCrdtMsg): no Dart preimage, lives OUTSIDE
  out/csharp, so the codeconv regen oracle never names it as an output.

  References glp_link ONLY (FrameCodec + TcpTransport) — this is what lets the
  thin client stay free of a direct runtime reference (R7): both GlpEngineHost
  and GlpReplClient share these payload types without the client pulling in the
  engine surface.

  TargetFramework note: plan.md says .NET 8. It was net10.0 for the reason below,
  and is now net11.0 by ENGINEER MANDATE (2026-08-27): ".NET 11 and C# 15 latest
  preview ... c#15 opt in approved and mandated". The pin lives in the repo root:
  global.json (SDK 11.0.100-preview.7.26381.103) + Directory.Build.targets
  (LangVersion=preview, which is the ONLY way to reach C# 15 — see that file).

  The original constraint still holds in shape: a project cannot reference a
  higher target than its own, and every project in the reference chain moved
  together (23 csproj, net10.0 -> net11.0, all 10 test projects green: 1111
  tests, 0 failed). Recorded as a plan deviation in specs/061-.../baseline.md.

  ONE MIXED EDGE, deliberate: out/csharp/glp_runtime_net is GENERATED by codeconv
  and is still net10.0. net11.0 referencing net10.0 is legal and builds clean, so
  it is not broken — but retargeting it means changing the GENERATOR, not this
  tree, or the next regeneration silently reverts it.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net11.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>GlpRuntime.SplitProtocol</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>glp_split_protocol</AssemblyName>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <WarningsAsErrors>CS0649;CS0169</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\glp_link\GlpLink.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="GlpEngineHost.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
